# Current Sol xhigh Comparison

**Decision class:** `COMPUTATIONAL_SYSTEMS_COMPARISON_ONLY`  
**Sensory winner:** `NOT TESTED`  
**DeepLuna comparison:** `NOT RUN — exact-project route BLOCKED_BUDGET_UNSAFE`

## Outcome

The revised twenty-arm studio is demonstrably cleaner as a formulation and execution system: all 20 current-inventory builds parse at exactly 4,500 µL, pass the 10 µL raw-stock floor, use one explicit Ethylene Brassylate musk, exclude all lost tinctures, resolve live inventory through the approved overlay, and complete the native family pipelines with zero hard gate failures.

That is **not evidence that any arm smells better, is closer to YSL, or is more hedonic than the frozen Sol formulas**. The new L’Homme arms are more top-heavy in the modeled OAV distribution than the frozen Sol L’Homme baseline, while the Sol La Nuit baseline also has zero hard failures. Physical balanced-order testing remains the only valid preference comparison.

## Fresh 305 K Native Runs

| Arm | Rows | Raw µL | PASS | WARN | FAIL | Overall | Opening OAV T/H/B | Drydown OAV T/H/B | Musk design |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|
| Frozen Sol L’Homme xhigh | 22 | 6000 | 112 | 16 | 1 | FAIL | 67.2/21.7/11.1 | 31.0/45.6/23.4 | 3: Zenolide, Habanolide, Ambrettolide (10% in DPG) |
| Frozen Sol La Nuit xhigh | 20 | 4500 | 110 | 19 | 0 | WARN | 56.8/29.2/13.9 | 23.6/46.1/30.3 | 2: Habanolide, Romandolide |
| Twenty-arm studio | 18–26 | 4,500 each | 108–113 | 16–21 | **0 each** | WARN (20/20) | model-specific; see summary | model-specific; see summary | 1 each: Ethylene Brassylate |

Frozen Sol L’Homme’s sole hard failure is the new execution rule: `Basil EO (India, Ocimum Basilicum)=8.0uL below 10.0 uL raw-stock floor; prepare a verified dilution and rebase the formula before compounding`

Gate totals are diagnostics, not a perfume ranking.

## What the program repair changed

- Corrected natural-mixture routing for current inventory labels and added explicit literature-partial proxy authority for lemon, black pepper, ginger, spike lavender, and tonka. These are not user-lot measurements.
- Corrected natural composite evaporation so constituent ratios evolve over time rather than remaining frozen into drydown.
- Made serialized `note_distribution` OAV-weighted and retained active-mass distribution separately.
- Reconciled composite natural vapor ppm, effective ODT, and OAV in every material row.
- Classified composite-natural `derived_effective:` ODTs as low-authority evidence so dominant proxy naturals now produce an explicit warning instead of a false clean pass.
- Corrected Bergamot FCF oil Sicilian from heart to top classification.
- Corrected the climate gate’s Kelvin/Celsius unit error: 305 K is modeled as 31.85 °C and ~2.20× VP versus 22 °C, not 157,728×.
- Stopped the legacy evaluator from parsing appended OAV tables as formula ingredients and corrected its 0.1% dilution parser.
- Enforced the user’s 10 µL minimum raw-stock dose for neat and diluted rows; the nine 8 µL Black Pepper sockets were rebased to 10 µL with a 2 µL Tonkarome-stock offset.
- Added native `ysl_lhomme` and `ysl_la_nuit_de_lhomme` family contracts while retaining name-first optimization and claim ceilings.
- Made native family-identity drift release-blocking; a formula that loses the L’Homme or La Nuit architecture can no longer be demoted to an advisory warning.

## Formula-level diagnosis

- **L’Homme family:** modeled openings are citrus/aromatic-dominant and often show thin OAV hearts. This is a risk to be tested, not a mandate to add more ingredients. Adaptation, suppression, and lot-specific naturals are not physically calibrated.
- **LH‑04 Apple Pie:** apple materials are modeled strongly, but 2-acetylpyrazine, cinnamaldehyde, and vanillin remain threshold-limited or authority-limited. The pastry module needs a carrier-matched constant-total omission/addition test; increasing a water-threshold proxy would be unjustified.
- **LH‑06 Violet Leaf Silk:** neat beta-ionone was a true design defect. Replacing its 20 µL neat row with 20 µL of owned 0.1% TEC stock reduces modeled OAV from ~8,595 to ~8.6 and restores literal violet leaf as the named accent.
- **La Nuit family:** current models preserve cardamom/lavender/cedar/coumarin architecture, but several arms remain top-heavy in headspace and warnings consistently flag sparse intimate diffusion. Unknown musk stock bases prevent a justified Habanolide/Romandolide substitution.
- **LN‑05 Immortelle Nuit:** Immortelle 10% is modeled through a composite proxy, but its stock basis remains `VERIFY_FIRST`; curry/maple restraint and liking are physically untested.

